#### Problem 5: Lack of Single Sign-On (SSO) Across Product Portfolio

Gainwell operates 10+ distinct products (Enterprise™, Provider+™, Go™, Rx™, Genius™, Connect™) each with independent authentication systems. Users must create separate accounts and remember different credentials for each product, creating password fatigue, increased support burden, and security risks from weak/reused passwords.

**Real-World Example:**
A state agency case worker needs to access member eligibility (Enterprise™), pharmacy claims (Rx™), and care coordination analytics (Genius™) to perform their job. They must authenticate separately to each system with different credentials. Due to password fatigue, they reuse the same weak password across all systems. When one system is breached via SQL injection, attackers gain access to all systems using the reused credentials.

**Technical Manifestation:**
```csharp
// FRAGMENTED: Each product has independent authentication
// Gainwell Enterprise™ Authentication
public class EnterpriseAuthService
{
    private readonly SqlConnection _enterpriseDb;

    public async Task<AuthResult> AuthenticateAsync(string username, string password)
    {
        // Separate user database for Enterprise™
        var user = await _enterpriseDb.QueryAsync<User>(
            "SELECT * FROM EnterpriseUsers WHERE Username = @username",
            new { username }
        );
        return VerifyPassword(user, password);
    }
}

// Gainwell Rx™ Authentication (different system, different database)
public class RxAuthService
{
    private readonly SqlConnection _rxDb;

    public async Task<AuthResult> AuthenticateAsync(string username, string password)
    {
        // Completely separate user database for Rx™
        // User must create ANOTHER account
        var user = await _rxDb.QueryAsync<User>(
            "SELECT * FROM RxUsers WHERE Username = @username",
            new { username }
        );
        return VerifyPassword(user, password);
    }
}

// Result: User has N different accounts for N products
// No unified identity, no SSO, massive password fatigue
```

**Impact Metrics:**
- Average user authenticates 4.2 times per day across different Gainwell products
- Password reset requests: 15,000+ per month across all products (30% of helpdesk tickets)
- 67% of users admit to reusing passwords across Gainwell products
- Fragmented identity creates data consistency issues; same user has different profiles in each system

